  keySpec: "4.1 m diameter  \xB7  8.6 t propellant"
  summary: Built by ESA and Airbus, this is Orion's engine room. It carries the propulsion,
    propellant, electrical power, water, oxygen and thermal radiators, and supplies
    all of it to the crew module through an umbilical.
  whyItMatters: "It is jettisoned before re-entry and burns up. Keeping everything
    that does not need to survive 2,760\_\xB0C outside the part that does means the
    heat shield protects 8.5 tonnes instead of the full 26-tonne stack."
  narration: {fileID: 0}
